# Test-traffic exclusion list. One SID per line; everything after # is a comment.
# Copy to excluded_sids.txt (gitignored) and fill in the real ones at deploy time.
#
# These SIDs are DROPPED from every researcher measure AND from the pseudonymised
# export -- non-real participant streams (prod-UAT rehearsals, e2e runs, hand-seeded
# test rows) that would otherwise pollute the analysis and the dashboards.
#
# Unlike enrolled_sids.txt (an ALLOW-list that only filters when it is populated and
# a roster is active), this is a DENY-list that applies WHENEVER it names anyone,
# regardless of roster state -- which is what lets it clean test traffic out of the
# roster-off live deployment. Absent/empty file => nothing is excluded (the default).
#
# Matching is by canonical SID (the same _canon_sid rule as everywhere else), so a
# stream recorded under EITHER the numeric or the check-letter form of one SID is
# excluded by naming either form here.
#
# Populate from a box query at the Saturday deploy (the ~6 excess prod-UAT
# participant_ids + the 2 test questionnaire_feedback streams). Examples:
#
# 12345678    # prod-UAT rehearsal account (numeric form)
# 87654321D   # e2e smoke-test stream (check-letter form -- folds to 87654321)
